To create the trivia webpage, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript [1]. Here's how to implement the color changes for the buttons and the text field:

1.  **Multiple-Choice Questions:**

    *   In your `index.html` file, create a multiple-choice question using `h3` for the question text and `button` elements for each answer choice [1].
    *   Use JavaScript to add logic that changes the button colors when clicked [1]. You can use `document.querySelectorAll` to select all the buttons [1].
    *   If the user clicks an incorrect answer, change the button's color to red and display "Incorrect" [1].
    *   If the user clicks the correct answer, change the button's color to green and display "Correct!" [1].
2.  **Free Response Question:**

    *   In `index.html`, add a text-based question using an `h3` heading, an `input` field for the user's response, and a `button` to confirm the answer [1].
    *   Use JavaScript to change the text field's color when the user confirms their answer [1]. You can use `document.querySelector` to select a single HTML element [1].
    *   If the answer is incorrect, change the text field to red and display "Incorrect" [1].
    *   If the answer is correct, change the text field to green and display "Correct!" [1].

Here's an example of how you can change the background color of HTML elements using JavaScript [2]:

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>background</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <button id="red">R</button>
    <button id="green">G</button>
    <button id="blue">B</button>
    <script>
      let body = document.querySelector("body");
      document.querySelector("#red").addEventListener("click", function () {
        body.style.backgroundColor = "red";
      });
      document.querySelector("#green").addEventListener("click", function () {
        body.style.backgroundColor = "green";
      });
      document.querySelector("#blue").addEventListener("click", function () {
        body.style.backgroundColor = "blue";
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
```

In this example, clicking the buttons changes the background color of the page [2, 3]. You can adapt this code to change the background color of the buttons and text field in your trivia webpage [2].
